refined_question:
For each s ∈ (1/2, 3/2), let γ := 1 - 1/(2s), and let L_{γ,1,s} be the optimal constant in the critical fractional Lieb–Thirring inequality for the self-adjoint operator (-Δ)^s + V on L^2(R),
Tr(((-Δ)^s + V)_-)^{γ} ≤ L_{γ,1,s} ∫_R V_-(x) dx,
valid for all real-valued potentials V with V_- ∈ L^1(R). If L^{(1)}_{γ,1,s} denotes the corresponding one-particle constant, i.e. the optimal constant in the inequality obtained by replacing the left-hand side by |λ_1(( -Δ)^s + V)|^{γ} (equivalently, the contribution of a single negative eigenvalue), is it true that
L_{1-1/(2s),1,s} = L^{(1)}_{1-1/(2s),1,s}
for every s ∈ (1/2, 3/2)? ([link.springer.com](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00220-024-05216-y))
